<title>BELGIUM: Commission air slot rule change postponed.</title>
<headline>Commission air slot rule change postponed.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has postponed once again plans for a revision of Regulation 95/93/EEC governing the sale of take-off and landing slots at EU airports, a Commission official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Plans by European Transport Commissioner Neil Kinnock to revise existing EU rules banning the sale of slots have repeatedly faltered faced with opposition from Competition Commissioner Karel Van Miert.</p>
<p>The file was slated for discussion at the Commission's weekly meeting on May 7 but has once again slipped off the agenda with no compromise in sight, the official said.</p>
</text>
